  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.7.1: the description of the package says that it is a community project, not affiliated with Chroma, and the tags have chroma-cloud. 2.7.0: for Chroma Cloud, the Search API: ChromaCollectionClient.Search with ChromaSearch, ChromaRank (Knn, SparseKnn, Rrf and the arithmetic of ranks) and ChromaSearchGroupBy; sparse vectors in metadata, ChromaSparseVector, and the schema of a collection with sparse vector indexes, ChromaCollectionSchema and ChromaCollection.SparseVectorIndexes; ChromaBm25, the BM25 function of Chroma, with the same vectors as its Python client; Add, Update and Upsert compute the BM25 vectors that the schema declares, and SparseKnn takes a text, as the Python client does; new ChromaClient(uri) and new ChromaClient(options), with an HttpClient of their own that Dispose closes. 2.6.0: the rest of the v2 API: ChromaWhereDocumentOperator.Regex and NotRegex; Delete(ChromaDelete) by filters, with a limit and the count of the deleted records; ModifyConfiguration, for the settings of the index of the collection; Healthcheck; Count(ChromaReadLevel); ChromaClient.WithTenantAndDatabaseFromIdentity; for Chroma Cloud Fork, ForkCount, GetIndexingStatus, AttachFunction, GetAttachedFunction, DetachFunction, GetCollectionByCrn and UpdateTenant. XML documentation in the package. Fixed: ChromaCollection.Space also reads the space that Chroma Cloud sends in the spann configuration; the validation errors of the 0.x servers are the message of the exception. 2.5.0: embeddings in base64 where the server declares supports_base64_encoding; WithBatchSplitting(maxBatchSize) for servers like Chroma Cloud, which declares 1000 but takes 300 records per write; ChromaException.ErrorType; CollectionExists also by a NotFoundError about a collection. 2.4.1: works in applications published with trimming or NativeAOT: serialization with metadata generated at build time, IsAotCompatible. All the releases: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/releases. Tested versions: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client/blob/main/docs/COMPATIBILITY.md. Migration from 1.x: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Client#migrating-from-chromadbclient-1x",
